                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Major insurance companies are gaming the Obamacare system through the Medical Loss Ratio (MLR) rule, requiring health insurers to spend at least 80% of the premiums they collect on medical care and quality improvements for patients\u2014if they spend less, they have to issue rebates to customers.\n\nUnlike the free market, where competition drives companies to deliver better services at lower costs, this rule eliminates the incentive to cut costs because higher medical spending enables higher insurer revenue.\n\nCongress shouldn\u2019t throw more money at failed Obamacare. Let Biden\u2019s COVID-era subsidies EXPIRE!",
